 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the\nqualifications of members of the Battery Park city authority",
    "basePrintNo": "S7284",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7284-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1973, Pub Auth L (as proposed in S. 130-B and A. 4002-A)",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7284\n\nSPONSOR: KAVANAGH\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend to amend the public authorities law,\nin relation to the qualifications of members of the Battery Park city\nauthority\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would amend Chapter 473 of the Laws of 2017 to ensure that\nboard members of the Battery Park City Authority have appropriate expe-\nrience and recuse themselves in the event of a conflict of interest.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Amends § 1973 of the Public Authorities Law to provide that\nall board members of the Battery Park City Authority shall: (1) recuse\nthemselves in the event of a conflict of interest, consistent with\nexisting law and guidance; and (2) have relevant experience in at least\none of the following areas - real estate, corporate board, financial,\nlegal, urban planning or design, architectural, governmental or securi-\nty.\n\nSection 2. Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChapter 473 of the Laws of 2017 required that at least 2 of the 7 board\nmembers of the Battery Park City Authority shall be residents of Battery\nPark City. This bill would require the individual residents - as well as\nall other board members - to have appropriate experience to serve on the\nboard and to recuse themselves in the event of a conflict of interest.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill to amend Chapter 473 of the Laws of 2017.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date as Chapter 473 of the Laws\nof 2017, which was December 18, 2017.\n",
